.TH sway-things-hook-launch 1 "" "Sway Things 0.6.0" "Sway Things Manual"
.SH NAME
sway\-things\-hook\-launch \- Start an installed app by its desktop file ID, as its desktop entry says (in a terminal if it asks for one): the autostart entries of Sway Things that are apps run this
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsway\-things hook launch\fR [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIID\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Start an installed app by its desktop file ID, as its desktop entry says (in a terminal if it asks for one): the autostart entries of Sway Things that are apps run this
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR [default: auto]
Controls when to use color
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIID\fR>
The desktop file ID, e.g. `org.mozilla.firefox.desktop`
